# Copy to backend/.env for local overrides (loaded automatically via python-dotenv).
# None of these are required for local dev - the app has safe fallbacks:
#   - No DATABASE_URL -> uses a local SQLite file (backend/local_dev.db)
#   - No JWT_SECRET_KEY -> uses an insecure dev default (BLOCKED in production, see below)
#   - No SMTP_HOST -> email verification is skipped entirely (accounts auto-verify)
#   - No GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID -> Google sign-in button won't work, email/password still does

# ---- Required in production (ENVIRONMENT=production) - app refuses to start without these ----
# ENVIRONMENT=production
# JWT_SECRET_KEY=generate-with-openssl-rand-hex-32
# ALLOWED_ORIGINS=https://your-frontend.vercel.app

# ---- Database (Railway injects this automatically once Postgres is attached) ----
# DATABASE_URL=postgresql://user:password@host:5432/dbname

# ---- OSRM ----
# OSRM_URL=http://osrm.railway.internal:5000

# ---- Google Sign-In ----
# GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=your-client-id.apps.googleusercontent.com

# ---- Email (optional - see DEPLOYMENT.md section 0) ----
# SMTP_HOST=smtp.gmail.com
# SMTP_PORT=587
# SMTP_USER=you@gmail.com
# SMTP_PASSWORD=your-app-password
# FROM_EMAIL=you@gmail.com
# FRONTEND_URL=https://your-frontend.vercel.app
